<http://data.silknow.org/event/3a3bee38-fb77-394d-9ad0-bfe36c779f13>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Purchased. Registered File no. 1930/7422.\n\nHistorical significance: This is a classic Cycladic bed curtain with a vertical border on each width of linen and a wide ornamental border at top. The elements of the pattern, however, suggest the Dodecanese (alternate King and Queen patterns and hexagons). It is just possible that this is a red curtain from Patmos. Other possibilities would be Amorgos or Melos."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9ec75435-a2da-3f22-bb74-5a0ead063a6b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Purchased. Registered File no. 1930/7422.\n\nHistorical significance: This is a classic Cycladic bed curtain with a vertical border on each width of linen and a wide ornamental border at top. The elements of the pattern, however, suggest the Dodecanese (alternate King and Queen patterns and hexagons). It is just possible that this is a red curtain from Patmos. Other possibilities would be Amorgos or Melos."@en .

